le, v4.5.stable, later v4.5.beta snapshots\n- Not reproducible in: v4.5.dev5.official [64b09905c], v4.4.stable, earlier v4.5.dev snapshots\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.1.stable - macOS Sequoia (15.6.1) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M2 (Apple8) - Apple M2 (8 threads) - 16.00 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen double clicking an editable TreeItem, the size of the popup is too large. This only happens when the window's `content_scale_factor` is greater than 0 and `embed_subwindows` is disabled.\n\nScreenshot before editing tree with content_scale_factor set to 2:\n<img width=\"282\" height=\"188\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7e165576-8c54-4c15-9651-3a7f084e2e20\" />\nand when tree is being edited, with the popup twice as tall as it should be:\n<img width=\"282\" height=\"181\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b700cd50-b6b9-4049-b3e7-87b41da3a629\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a scene with a Tree node\n2. Give the Tree at least one editable TreeItem\n3. Set Embed Subwindows to false in Project Settings\n4. Set Display/Window/Stretch/Scale to 2.0 in Project Settings\n5. Ensure the editor's Game view has 'Embed Game on Next Play' disabled\n6. Run game and double click to edit TreeItem\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[tree-test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22963433/tree-test.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/ow